  whatwrong="In `routes/verification.ts` the public, no-login `POST /api/verification/verify` has a lookup block `try { ... } catch (dbErr) { logger.warn('Verification lookup failed', ...); return res.json({ verified: false, error: 'Verification lookup failed' }); }`. Strategy 2 (a body with a `documentId`) answers a found row with `return respondExistenceOnly(rows[0], '...')`. `respondExistenceOnly` is an `async` function, and the call is NOT awaited: a throw inside it (a field read of the row, `buildCertification`, the response write) is a rejected promise that is returned out of the `try`, so the lookup catch never sees it, and the outer catch never sees it either. The handler's promise rejects and, under Express 4, the request gets NO RESPONSE, even for an ordinary Error (QA gate 106, G106-F2, measured at base and head). Every other throw inside that `try` (the lookup query, the strategy-1 branches, which are awaited or synchronous) is caught and answered 200 'Verification lookup failed'. The fix is `return await respondExistenceOnly(`: the one line changes and nothing else; the success path returns the same value.",
  callers="CALLERS: the route is mounted by `index.ts` at `/api/verification` and is PUBLIC (no login; the API gateway rate-limits it); it is called by HTTP clients only. WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the site): an ordinary Error thrown anywhere else inside the lookup `try` (for example the by-id lookup query rejecting, cell C1) is logged with `logger.warn('Verification lookup failed', { documentId, error: <message> })` and answered `200 { verified: false, error: 'Verification lookup failed' }`. After the fix an ordinary Error (or a thrown string) thrown inside `respondExistenceOnly` gets exactly that, byte for byte, and the cells assert the status, the body, the logged call and that no write was issued. Today: NO ANSWER (the cell's client times out after 1.5 s) and nothing is logged by the handler. Persisted state: none in either case: `respondExistenceOnly` only reads (one tenant lookup SELECT and read-only lineage walks, each in their own try); the handler has no heal or audit write on this strategy; the cells assert `$executeRaw` is never called. Disclosure: the 200 body is a constant with no field of the document, the caller or the error; no new text reaches an anonymous caller (it receives an answer where it received none). The success path is untouched (cell C2 pins the existence-only answer: `verified: false`, `integrityVerified: false`, no verdict). A throw AFTER the response was already sent would make the catch's own `res.json` throw and fall to the outer catch exactly as for any other position in that try: nothing new. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state:** a throw inside the by-id existence answer now produces the lookup catch's ordinary answer (200 'Verification lookup failed' plus one warn log line) instead of leaving the request unanswered. A thrown value whose `message` cannot be read is NOT covered by this pass (the catch's own `dbErr?.message` read is pass O78-P2, KS-1939 as well): until that lands such a value reaches the outer catch's constant 500 as it does at every other position in this try. Recommended tier 1 (public verification surface; Kam's tier-1-with-Opus-gate ruling).",
