  whatwrong="In `routes/verification.ts` the lookup block of the public, no-login `POST /api/verification/verify` ends in `catch (dbErr: any) { logger.warn('Verification lookup failed', { documentId, error: dbErr?.message }); return res.json({ verified: false, error: 'Verification lookup failed' }); }`. If the thrown value is a revoked Proxy, `dbErr?.message` itself throws a TypeError inside the catch; if it is an Error whose `message` getter throws, the getter's throw escapes the same way. The new throw reaches the OUTER catch, which answers HTTP 500 'Verification failed' instead of the 200 'Verification lookup failed' that an ordinary Error gets (QA gate 106, G106-F1, measured at base and head). The fix reads the SAME expression into a local `reason` inside its own `try` and sets the constant `'unreadable thrown value'` when the read throws; the log call then uses `reason`. **The `documentId` key and the log message text are NOT changed in this pass** (see the behaviour note).",
  callers="CALLERS: the route is mounted by `index.ts` at `/api/verification` and is PUBLIC (no login; gateway rate limit); HTTP clients only. WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the site): the lookup catch logs one warn line `{ documentId, error: <message> }` and answers `200 { verified: false, error: 'Verification lookup failed' }`. After the fix an unreadable thrown value gets exactly that outcome, with the constant `unreadable thrown value` as the logged error; the status, the body and the logged keys are the ordinary Error's, and the cells assert them (and that no write was issued). Today (unreadable): the catch throws, the outer catch answers 500 'Verification failed' and logs an error line. Persisted state: none in either case (the lookup is read-only on this strategy; no heal or audit write is issued here; the cells assert `$executeRaw` is never called). Disclosure: the 200 body is a constant; the response never carries the thrown text; the logged value for an unreadable thrown value is the constant. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state:** for an unreadable thrown value only, a failure inside the lookup block of `POST /verify` is answered 200 'Verification lookup failed' (as for an ordinary Error) instead of 500 'Verification failed'; readable values (an Error, a string) log byte-identically to today, including `error: undefined` for a thrown string. NOT changed, and left for a separate decision (ks1346, G106-F1/F7): the caller-supplied `documentId` is still logged in this line, and a readable error message is still logged verbatim. Recommended tier 1 (public verification surface; Kam's tier-1-with-Opus-gate ruling).",
